# Input/output logic (Makinson & van der Torre 2000): G = {(a,b), (b,c)},
# input A = {a}. Simple-minded output out1(G,A) = Cn({b}): c is not output
# (outputs are not fed back as inputs); reusable output out3 adds c.
# AIDA has no closure operator and no output operation: a norm (a,x) is a
# rule from the input a to the output atom Ox. Which outputs exist is
# fixed by which rules are written: here the out1 reading.
lk.
declare A, B, Ob, Oc : bool.
declare a : (A).
declare n_ab : (A -> Ob).
declare n_bc : (B -> Oc).
argument ob : (Ob).
cut (A -> Ob) t.
axiom n_ab.
elim.
axiom a.
axiom t.
dixi.
argument oc : (Oc).
cut (B -> Oc) t.
axiom n_bc.
elim.
next.
axiom t.
dixi.
